Package: pollinatoR
Title: Uncertainty-Aware Pollinator-Dependence Analytics for Exclusion
    Experiments
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Max", "Moldovan", email = "max.moldovan@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: Tools for estimating the contribution of insect pollinators to
    crop yield from pollinator-exclusion experiments (open versus caged, and
    related contrasts). Provides model-based average and conditional treatment
    effects with propagated uncertainty, uncertainty-aware dependence indices
    (a defensible replacement for bare ratio indices such as the Relative
    Interaction Index), a within-between decomposition that shields the
    exposure-by-treatment estimand from site-level confounders such as an
    unobserved genotype, a permutation guard against the spurious correlation
    that arises when a dependence index is regressed on a yield axis that shares
    a term, and structural data-integrity checks. The methods are general to
    open-versus-exclusion designs across crops and are not specific to any one
    study. Developed with support from the Grains Research and Development
    Corporation (GRDC project USQ2401-002RTX) and Analytics for the Australian
    Grains Industry (AAGI).
